            "review_title": "Review at DWok Restaurant",
            "review_text": "tth967\nSingapore, Singapore5 contributions\n0\nDelicious Singaporean Food in Hanoi\nMay 2015 • Friends\nI was in Hanoi for a business trip and was invited to DWok restaurant for dinner. Upon reaching the place, found the ambience inside the restaurant bright and clean with young and cheerful staff providing great service. Tried their signature dishes, Hotplate BBQ Prawns, Salted Egg Cuttlefish, Deep Fried Dark Sauce Fish and my favourite Chill Crab. The freshness and level of the food served were excellent. The BBQ prawns were juicy and appetizing, the cuttlefish were tender and evenly coated with flavourful salted eggs. Deep fried fish was crispy on the outside but succulent on the inside. Best among all was the Chilli crab that came with a very savoury gravy that enhances the sweetness of the crab meat. This is one of the best restaurant I had been to in Hanoi and will most definitely go there again. I strongly recommend that anyone ,who enjoy good value and delicious food with a Singaporean flavour, to try it out.\nRead more\nValue\nService\nFood\nReview collected in partnership with this restaurant \nWritten October 11, 2015",
